# Poison Rhythm Component Standards

## Atomic layers (Photoshop-style)

Compose UI from small layers. Prefer **one root HTML element per component** (or a documented layout role). Larger screens are **composers** that stack atoms and molecules; side effects live in hooks.

```
atoms (ui/)     → one element: Button, IconButton, Caption, Stack, Row
molecules       → compose atoms: DescribedOptionCard, MeasuresPlayPauseButton, ModalActions, MeasureCarouselChrome
composers       → wire context + hooks: DifficultyControls, PlayModeControls, MeasureSlider, ShowNotes, Body
hooks           → interaction / playback: useOutsideDismiss, useMeasuresPlayPauseChrome, useMeasurePlaybackSync, useHoverPinPopover, …
```

- **Do not** invent raw `<button className=…>` in feature composers — use `@/components/ui` or existing control atoms
- **Variants over className** on shared components
- **No superfluous wrappers**: an atom must own a real element or an intentional layout role (`Stack` / `Row` with `gap`)
- Context stays on composers; atoms/molecules take explicit props

## File Organization

```
src/components/
├── ui/                    # Elemental shared primitives (Button, IconButton, Caption, Stack, Row)
├── controls/              # PlayModeControls + difficulty / DifficultyControls composers
├── layout/                # App chrome, overlays, metronome UI
│   ├── about/
│   ├── button/
│   ├── metronome/
│   ├── settings/          # Settings panels + setting atoms (EnableToggle, When, …)
│   └── …
├── measures/              # Measure carousel atoms + MeasureSlider / MeasuresSection composers
└── poison/                # Poison section layers + PoisonSection composer
```

## Component Structure Guidelines

### Avoid Superfluous Wrappers

- **Remove unnecessary wrapper divs**: Don't create wrapper divs that add DOM complexity without benefit
- **Simplify component structure**: Remove redundant nesting when possible
- **Keep meaningful wrappers**: Retain wrappers that serve styling, semantic or layout purposes (`Stack`, `Row`, `Section`, `PoisonMeasureFrame`)

### Spacing Guidelines

- **Avoid `space-*` utilities**: Don't use `space-x-*` or `space-y-*` — they rely on margin-based spacing
- **Use flex/gap spacing**: Prefer `Stack` / `Row` atoms, or `flex flex-col gap-*` / `flex items-center gap-*`
- **Maintain visual consistency**: Spacing changes should preserve the intended layout

## Core Components

### App (root)

- **Uses**: `GameProvider`; renders Header, Body, Footer; mounts `IntroTutorialProvider` + `IntroModalHost` beside the tree
- **State**: Round and measures via `useGame` in child sections. First-visit welcome persists via `poison-rhythm-intro-seen` only when the student opts out; **Settings → Mode → Welcome Tutorial** replays it. `StatusToastAnnouncer` + `ToastHost` announce screen-chrome preference diffs; `Body` toasts New / Reuse; Settings suppresses preference announcements while open

### Body

- **Purpose**: Main game composition
- **Uses**: `useSoftDisableFocus` for New → Play focus guidance; renders PoisonSection, MeasuresSection, PlayControls; owns the single `DisplayModeModal` via `useDisclosure`
- **No props**: Reads game state from context

### AppTitle

- **Purpose**: Header brand title + Mode icon
- **Uses**: `AboutPoisonRhythmButton` and `ModeBadgeTrigger` both call `openAbout`; `resolveGameModeHudBadge` from settings
- **Layout**: Mode icon sits immediately to the right of **Poison Rhythm**; Mode trigger accessible name is **Mode and Difficulty** (distinct from the brand title)

### PlayModeControls (composer)

- **Purpose**: Play Mode section independent of Difficulty
- **Uses**: `PlayModeFramedBlock` (About) or `PlayModeOptionList` (Settings `framed={false}`)
- **Global bindings**: `PlayModeOptionList` → `useSetting('gameMode'|'endless')` + `handleNewRound({ gameMode })` on mode change

### DifficultyControls (composer)

- **Purpose**: Difficulty section + help modal only (play mode is separate)
- **Uses**: `DifficultyFramedBlock` / `DifficultySettingsBlock`, `DifficultyHelpModal`, `useDisclosure` (local open/close only)
- **Global bindings**: `DifficultySlider` → `usePendingDifficulty`
- **Variants**: `framed` (About section box) vs compact Settings block (`framed={false}`)
- **Note**: Brand title and Mode icon both open About (Play Mode then Difficulty). Settings → Mode mirrors both groups. After the host modal closes with a pending difficulty change, `PendingDifficultyProvider` regenerates the round; `DifficultyRegenAckHost` (App-level) shows a timed acknowledgement (`Modal` `dismissAfterMs`, no OK button).

### Modal (composer)

- **Purpose**: Shared dialog shell
- **Layers**: `ModalScrim`, `ModalPanel` (`size` / `fullWidth`), `ModalCloseButton` (`IconButton` `modalClose`), `ModalTitle`, `useModalFocusTrap`
- **Portal**: Renders via `createPortal(..., document.body)` so nested dialogs (Difficulty Help inside About or Settings) are not clipped by a parent `ModalPanel` `overflow` / `backdrop-filter` containing block. Non-`xl` panels use a definite `dvh` max-height and scroll the body; `useModalFocusTrap` only handles Escape/Tab for the topmost `.Modal`.
- **Props**: `open`, `onClose`, `title`, `ariaLabel`, `size`, `fullWidth`, optional `headerLeading` (upper-left slot; metronome mute) and `dismissAfterMs` (auto-close + `TimedNoticeProgress`)

### CornerModal / CornerButton

- **Variants**: `tone?: 'default' | 'muted'` (muted = dashed mid border for muted metronome); optional `dismissAfterMs` for the timed notice (Account). No `className` / `buttonClassName` passthrough
- **Hooks**: `useDisclosure`, `useDelayedClick` for single vs double-click open; optional `onOpenChange` (Settings uses this to suppress status toasts)

### ui/ atoms

- **Button**: text actions (`primary` | `secondary` | `ghost`); `grow` fills row space (`true` → flex-1, `'auto'` → flex-auto)
- **IconButton**: glyph/icon-only (`info` | `bare` | `circle` | `modalClose`); `circle` wraps round badges (Mode) so hover recolors the badge border instead of drawing an inset box
- **Caption**: muted helper `<p>` (`xs` | `sm`)
- **Stack** / **Row**: vertical / horizontal flex+gap layout layers

### PoisonSection (composer)

- **Purpose**: Poison rhythm and New/Reuse controls
- **Props**: `poisonRhythm`, `onNewPoison`, `onReusePoison`, `onOpenDisplayMode`, optional soft-disable focus helpers
- **Header**: `PoisonSectionHeader` (`slot: 'leading' | 'action'`) → visibility toggle / display trigger
- **Display Mode**: Grid / Notation / Scroll on the badge; modal owned by `Body` (not this section). Scroll is Guitar Hero–style highway (`ScrollHighway`); direction in `DisplayModeControls`; `CarouselNavButtons` uses `showSideNav={false}` in Scroll. In Scroll, poison stacks notation + grid via `PoisonReferenceViews`
- **Uses**: `PoisonMeasureContent` / `PoisonReferenceViews` / `PoisonMeasureFrame` / `HiddenPoisonOverlay`, Section, ControlButtons

### MeasuresSection / MeasureSlider

- **MeasuresSection**: Empty state or carousel; `MeasuresPracticeToggles` + `MeasuresSectionHeaderActions` (`VolumeMenu`); opens Body-owned `DisplayModeModal` in Bucket mode
- **MeasureSlider**: Presentational carousel; `live` on chrome for `data-testid="measure-slider"`; playback side effects in `useMeasurePlaybackSync`
- **Layers**: `NextMeasurePreview`, `CurrentMeasureDisplay` / `measure-phase-chrome` (`data-playback-phase`: idle / count-in / listening / playing — fixed `border-2`; Listening = dashed primary shell + ink notes, Playing = secondary glow shell + secondary notes, count-in faded), `CarouselNavButtons` (section chrome tabs before Previous Measure / Next Measure; first-measure delayed Play; last-measure New / Reuse / Play)

### MeasureGrid / MeasureCell

- **Purpose**: 16th-note grid with accent, sticking (L/R), poison overlay and playback highlighting
- **Composer**: Section composers (`MeasuresSection`, `PoisonMeasureContent`) call `useMeasureDisplayOptions` and pass `display: MeasureDisplayOptions` into `MeasureGrid` / `CurrentMeasureDisplay` / `MeasureHeightReserve`
- **Leaves**: `MeasureGrid` switches grid vs notation; `MeasureCellGrid` / `MeasureCell` / `MeasureNotation` take explicit props (no context); scroll mode uses `ScrollHighway` from `MeasureSlider`
- **Props**: `measure`, optional `richMeasure`, `playback`, `hidden`, `display` (render mode, subdivision, feedback/accent/sticking flags, metronome step)
- **Render modes**: `grid`, `notation`, or `scroll` (SVG notation via `display.renderMode`; scroll uses `ScrollHighway`)
- **Layout**: Four pedagogical beats; wraps to **2×2** beat groups below `sm`
- **Overlays**: `RhythmAccentMark` / `RhythmAccentOverlay`; `RhythmStickingOverlay`

### Section / SectionTitle

- **Section**: Wrapper with title, optional `headerLeading` / `headerAction`, children
- **SectionTitle**: Section heading used inside Section

### Settings (layout/settings)

- **SettingsOverlay**: Three tabs — Mode, Sound, Colors (`SettingsTabs`)
- **GameSettingsPanel** / **SoundSettingsPanel** / **ColorSettingsPanel**: compose setting atoms (`Mode` includes Display; `Sound` includes feedback; `Colors` = `ColorAccentSettings`)
- **Colors:** `ColorAccentSettings` owns prefs + theme + `useColorRoleSelection` / `usePaletteContrast`; prop-drives `ColorPairPreview`, `ContrastScoreMeter` → `ThemeScoreRow`, `CrayonTray` (memoized grades on role + partner hex) → `CrayonTraySleeve` → `CrayonSwatch`, `SuggestedPairings` → `SuggestedPairingRow`, `SwapColorRolesButton`, `ColorRoleTile`
- **Settings binders:** keyed `useSetting(key)` (store subscription), `useUpdateSetting` (full blob), `usePlaybackMute(channel)` (`metronome` / `playback` / `preview`), mute / count-in composers, `MetronomeTempoSlider` via `useMetronomeTempo` + shared `TickedRangeInput`, `PlayModeOptionList`, `DifficultySlider` (also `TickedRangeInput`), `FeedbackToggles`, `DisplayModeControls`. Keep props for local UI (crayon edit role, modal open/close) or reusable atoms (`MuteToggle`, `EnableToggle`, `IconToggle`). Practice and Volume are mirrored: Measures `MeasuresPracticeToggles` / `VolumeMenu` + Settings → Mode / Sound.
- **Efficiency:** functional `useLocalStorage`; prefs split (complexity / sound / tempo); metronome tempo vs playback contexts; settings keyed store; Colors tray memo + theme isolation
- **SettingsGroup** / **ConditionalSettingsGroup**: Section dividers inside a tab
- **Setting utilities**: `SegmentedControl`, `When`, `useSetting`, `useUpdateSetting`
- **Fieldset**, **SegmentButton**, **SettingRow**, **EnableToggle** / **IconToggle** / **StatusIconToggle**, **FieldCaption**, **ThemeScoreRow**
- **Canonical grouping**: `SettingsGroup` (do not revive removed `SettingsSection` / `SettingsPanel`)

**Not in Settings as separate dials:** density or syncopation. Subdivision is mirrored (header ShowNotes + Settings → Mode).

## Guidelines

- **TypeScript types**: Prefer `type` over `interface` for props
- **Named exports**: Use `export function` or `export const` for components
- **Props**: Define a single props type per component when props are needed
- **Context over prop drilling**: Prefer `useGame` / `useSettings` in composers where state is global
- **Variants over className**: Do not accept `className` on shared components for styling customization
- **Imports**: Use barrel imports where available (`@/components/ui`, `@/components/controls`, …)
- **Type imports**: Keep `import type { ... }` on separate lines from component/value imports (Biome `useImportType` `separatedType`)

## Typography

- **Typographic apostrophe**: Use ’ instead of ' in all user-facing text
- **No Oxford comma**: Serial lists are `A, B and C` / `A, B or C` (not `A, B, and C` / `A, B, or C`)
- **Title Case**: Prefer Title Case for titles, control labels, `title`/`alt` and short `aria-label` names; sentence case for descriptions and hints

## Accessibility

- **Buttons**: Use `<button type='button'>` for actions; set `disabled` when not applicable
- **Labels**: Use clear, descriptive text and `aria-label` for icon-only controls
- **Contrast**: Use theme color utility classes and shared helpers from `lib/control-classes.ts` — see `.cursor/styling.mdc`
